---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, buildBreadcrumbLd } from '../lib/seo';

const title = 'Privacy Policy | PictoJXL';
const description =
  'PictoJXL privacy policy: image conversion stays in your browser. Details on contact email, ads, analytics, cookies, and retention for pictojxl.com.';

const jsonLd = [
  buildBreadcrumbLd([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Privacy Policy', path: '/privacy-policy' },
  ]),
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/privacy-policy" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <LegalPage
    title="Privacy Policy"
    description="What PictoJXL does—and does not—collect while you convert images on pictojxl.com."
    updated="October 27, 2026"
  >
    <p>
      <strong>Webwise Private Company Ltd</strong> (“Webwise,” “we,” “us”) operates
      <a href={absoluteUrl('/')}>pictojxl.com</a>, the PictoJXL browser studio (the “Service”). This
      policy explains our privacy practices. Using the Service means you accept these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>A. Local conversion promise</h2>
    <p>
      PictoJXL is built so encode and decode happen on your device. WebAssembly (and Web Workers when
      available) process your pictures inside the browser. We do not run a server-side conversion API
      that receives your image files, and we do not store converted outputs on our infrastructure.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your photos and graphics remain yours. Processing them with the tool does not transfer ownership
      to Webwise.
    </p>

    <h2>B. Data we may receive</h2>
    <h3>Messages you send</h3>
    <p>
      If you email <a href="mailto:support@pictojxl.com">support@pictojxl.com</a>, we receive whatever
      you put in that message—typically your address, name if provided, and the body—so we can reply.
    </p>
    <h3>Operational telemetry from hosting</h3>
    <p>
      Hosting, CDN, and security providers commonly see connection metadata: IP address, user agent,
      device class, OS hints, referrer, and timing. We use that to keep the site up, safe, and
      performant. It is not used to rebuild or inspect the contents of images you convert locally.
    </p>

    <h2>C. Advertising partners</h2>
    <p>
      The Service may show ads through Google AdSense or similar networks. Those partners can set
      cookies and use prior browsing activity (on this site or others) to decide which ads to show.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can adjust personalized advertising in
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
        >Google Ads Settings</a
      >. Google also documents partner data use at
      <a
        href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        target="_blank">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>D. Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We may enable analytics (Google Analytics or a privacy-minded alternative) to understand
      aggregate traffic and reliability. Typical signals include browser family, OS, coarse geography,
      and anonymized or aggregated usage. Where the product allows, IP anonymization may be turned on.
      Analytics is for operating and improving PictoJXL—not for reading your image pixels.
    </p>

    <h2>E. Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      Cookies and similar storage may support core site behavior and advertising. Categories and
      controls are described in the <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>F. Children</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their personal
      information. If you think a child contacted us with personal data, write to
      <a href="mailto:support@pictojxl.com">support@pictojxl.com</a> and we will delete it where
      appropriate.
    </p>

    <h2>G. How long we keep things</h2>
    <p>
      Image files from conversion are not retained on our servers because they are not uploaded for
      conversion. Support email and routine server or security logs are kept only as long as needed for
      support, security, legal duties, and ordinary business operations.
    </p>

    <h2>H. Links away from PictoJXL</h2>
    <p>
      Pages may link to third-party destinations (policy docs, ads settings, and similar). Their
      privacy practices are their own.
    </p>

    <h2>I. Visitors outside the United States</h2>
    <p>
      Webwise is a United States company. Site delivery and security processing may occur in the U.S.
      or in regions where our providers operate. Image conversion itself still runs in your browser,
      wherever you are.
    </p>

    <h2>J. Policy updates</h2>
    <p>
      We may revise this policy. The “Last updated” line on this page will change when we publish a
      revision. Continued use after an update means you accept the new version.
    </p>

    <h2>K. Reach us</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy questions about PictoJXL:<br />
      Webwise Private Company Ltd<br />
      <a href="mailto:support@pictojxl.com">support@pictojxl.com</a><br />
      <a href={absoluteUrl('/')}>https://pictojxl.com</a>
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</Layout>
